id: pm-rust-u4al
title: Deliver the Rust-native pm CLI and SDK
description: Implement an independent Rust CLI and library that operate on canonical pm workspaces without Node.js or Bun while preserving published pm data and agent-safety contracts.
type: Epic
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: agents,cli,interop,rust,sdk
created_at: "2026-08-06T21:15:44.282Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-27T04:06:08.180Z"
assignee: codex
claim_principal: codex
author: codex
estimated_minutes: 4800
acceptance_criteria: Rust-only CLI and SDK pass shared conformance fixtures against the latest published pm release; multi-process and real-branch tests prove no lost PM updates; publication remains disabled until privacy audit and maintainer approval
definition_of_ready: Canonical companion item pm-cli-website-204t is active and the latest published pm version is recorded
value: Single-binary low-overhead pm access for agents and native applications
impact: Exposes accidental TypeScript coupling and hardens the ecosystem's public contracts
outcome: Production-ready Rust implementation interoperable with canonical pm workspaces
why_now: pm 2026.8.21 is the current stable contract baseline for the independent implementation
reviewer: maintainer
risk: high
confidence: medium
sprint: 2026-08-native-mutations
release: 0.1.0-alpha.2
comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-22T11:46:49.625Z",codex,"Real-branch acceptance added as tests/branch_merge_contract.rs: two git branches mutate the same tracked item, then git merge reconciles through the published pm merge drivers installed from @unbrained/pm-cli 2026.8.21. Both mutations survive in the merged item and history."
  "2026-08-26T23:00:04.105Z",claude,"Coverage gate status measured precisely on 2026-08-27 UTC. The release-check gate asserts lines, functions, regions and branches are each exactly 100. Current measurement on the in-progress tree is lines 99.7556, functions 100, regions 99.6554, branches 99.5762, reproduced identically across three runs. The whole remaining gap is in src/mutation.rs: eight regions, four lines and one branch. history.rs, item.rs, main.rs and workspace.rs are all at 100 across every metric. main.rs reports branches as a dash rather than a percentage because it contains no branches at all, which is not a gap."
  "2026-08-26T23:00:04.663Z",claude,"Two measurement traps recorded so the next attempt does not pay for them again. First, llvm-cov's --lcov and --text exports report this tree as fully covered while --json and the summary table agree it is not; the exports cover a different file set, so --json is the one to trust and the one the gate reads. Second, the conformance tests skip when they cannot locate a published Node CLI, which looks like it would make the verdict environment-dependent. It does not: measured with PM_NODE_CLI set and unset, all four percentages are byte-identical, because the locator already resolves a CLI through PATH. I asserted that hypothesis before testing it and it was wrong."
  "2026-08-27T04:06:08.180Z",claude,"The coverage gate now passes end to end: lines, functions, regions and branches are each exactly 100, verified independently of the agent that produced the work by re-running llvm-cov and the gate's own jq assertion. The raise did not delete behaviour - the diff adds forty-seven error returns and removes one, and that one is a refactor of the same RecoveryConflict from a map_err combinator into an explicit match arm so each error path becomes a distinct coverable region. The justfile thresholds are untouched. Windows CI was broken by the new tests, which used std::os::unix::fs::PermissionsExt and Permissions::from_mode with no cfg guard, so the crate failed to compile on windows-latest with E0433 and E0599 while Linux was green; both tests now carry cfg(unix) exactly as the equivalent tests in read_contract.rs do, and coverage on Linux is unchanged at 100."
notes[3]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-06T21:15:44.282Z",codex,"Companion lineage: pm-cli-website-204t"
  "2026-08-07T11:39:16.643Z",codex,"Governance audit: CodeRabbit identified that an earlier metadata backfill on closed slice pm-rust-o2yr followed its release event. The append-only history is preserved rather than manually rewritten; the active epic is currently claimed by codex, and all review-driven implementation and PM evidence changes in this tranche remain under that active claim until verification completes."
  "2026-08-07T12:31:09.068Z",codex,Exact-head CodeRabbit review raised a 50% docstring warning because integration-test functions are outside cargo doc. Added high-signal rustdoc to both changed test functions while retaining the mandatory private-library rustdoc gate; no production behavior changed.
